0..79 Comment "/// A composite over a path typed at a stated lambda meets the composite at the"
80..100 Comment "/// lambda\'s reduct."
101..104 Comment "///"
105..182 Comment "/// `along`\'s type writes `F x`, so `along` at a stated lambda has the lambda"
183..253 Comment "/// applied at its endpoints. A composite over that path starts at the"
254..334 Comment "/// application. Passed to `composeHere`, whose type writes `Path.step p q`, its"
335..410 Comment "/// start meets the reduct `F x` or the application written again. A lambda"
411..497 Comment "/// whose body composes, `fun (q) { Path.step q g }`, meets a composite written apart."
498..501 Comment "///"
502..580 Comment "/// The conversion\'s code walk reads a call of a stated lambda as the lambda\'s"
581..660 Comment "/// body, its binder bound to the call\'s argument. Two composites written apart"
661..739 Comment "/// meet part by part. The kernel replays each declaration by its own reading."
740..743 Comment "///"
744..827 Comment "/// - see: #4073 — the checker refused a stated lambda applied against its reduct"
828..907 Comment "/// - see: #4065 — a call passed to a parameter, read as the value it returns"
908..960 Comment "/// - see: #3920 — one stated lambda written twice"
962..991 Comment "/// The action of `F` on `p`."
